 What is AWS Transit Gateway (TGW)?

AWS Transit Gateway is a central hub that connects multiple VPCs, on-premises networks, and VPN connections through a single gateway.

✅ Key Highlights:

Hub-and-Spoke Model: No need for complex VPC peering between every VPC.

Centralized Routing: Manage routes in one place using TGW route tables.

Highly Scalable: Supports thousands of VPC attachments.

Multi-Region Support: Inter-region peering available.


🔐 Use Cases:

Large-scale multi-VPC architectures.

Hybrid Cloud setups (AWS + on-prem).

Simplifying network management & reducing peering costs.


💡 Example: 10 VPCs need 100 peering connections in a mesh model. With TGW, only 10 attachments are required.
